  "raw_text": "20\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb-2Kings\n \n9:30\n):\n \nJezabel ba ai mawan ba pain aiskahkan\n \n–\n \nJezebel decorated her face (Jezebel put on makeup)\n \n/ Jezabel\ndecoró su rostro (Jezabel se maquilló))\n\nAisubaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be born, to give birth\n \n(\ndict,dictu\n)\n \n/ nacer, dar a luz (\ndict,dictu\n)\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nBaikaia\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb96\n):\n \nSaulo Tarso ra aisuban Rom uplika kum kan\n \n–\n \nSaul was born in Tarsus as a Roman citizen\n \n/\n \nSaulo naci\nó\n \nen Tarso\n\ncomo ciudadano romano\n)\n\nAisubi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be born\n \n/ nacer\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nAni ra aisubi takram?\n \n–\n \nWhere were you born?\n \n/ ¿Dónde naciste?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-08/20\n):\n \nBibi kum rayaka ba kau aisubi takras kra sin, Jehova nakra ra kulkanka tara brisa\n \n–\n \nEven the life of a\n\nbaby not yet born has great value in Jehovah’s eyes\n \n/\n \nIncluso la vida de un bebé que aún no ha nacido tiene un gran valor\na los ojos de Jehová)\n\nAisubi taka\nn\n \n(v\n-\n3p\n-\npast\n/pasado\n)\n \n–\n \nborn\n \n/\n \nnació\n, nacido\n\nAisubanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbirth\n \n/ nacimiento\n\nAisubanka yua\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbirthday, day of birth\n \n/ cumpleaños, día de nacimiento\n\nKli aisubi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto come to be born again\n \n/ venir a nacer de nuevo\n\nAitani\n \n(short form / forma corta:\n \nTani\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nenough, sufficient, perfect, exact, good, appropriate, in a proper way\n \n/\nsuficiente, perfecto, exacto, bueno, apropiado, de manera adecuada\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmy43\n) (Jehovah to Moses when he asked to cross the Jordan River into the promised land / Jehová a Moisés cuando pidió\ncruzar el río Jordán hacia la tierra prometida:\n \nAitani sa!\n \n–\n \nThat’s enough!\n \n/ ¡Es suficiente!)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu-09/19\n):\n \nDîa muni aitani sa ki swiaia Jehova mita wan tâ bribia?\n \n–\n \nWhy is it appropriate to allow Jehovah to lead us?\n \n/\nPor qué es apropiado permitir que Jehová nos guíe?)\n\nAitani kat\n \n(adj,adv)\n \n–\n \njust enough, at the appropriate amount, exactly, correctly, completely, sufficiently, perfectly\n\n/ lo suficiente, en la cantidad apropiada, exactamente, correctamente, completamente, suficientemente,\nperfectamente\n\nAitani lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto consider appropriate, to consider sufficient, to think of as good\n \n/ considerar apropiado,\npensar que es bueno\n\nDîa bri ba wal aitani lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto consider what you have as sufficient, to be content with what you\nhave\n \n/ considerar lo que tienes como suficiente, estar contento con lo que tienes\n\nAitnikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto lie down\n \n/ acostar, recostar\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nMeri ai luhpia aitnikan\n \n–\n \nMary laid her baby down\n \n/ María acostó a su bebé)\n\nÂ\ni\nulbra\n \n(Aiulbra)\n \n(\nsee/ver:\n \nUlbaia\n)\n \n(\nn\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente\n)\n \n–\n \nwriter,\n \nsecretary\n \n/\n \nescritor, secretario\n\n(Construct\n:\n \nÂ\ni\nulbrika\n)\n\nGaspil\n \nâ\ni\nulbra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nGospel writer\n \n/\n \nescritor del Evangelio\n\nLawana\n \nâ\ni\nulbra\n \n–\n \npsalmist\n \n/\n \nsalmista\n\nKangrigisan\n \nâ\ni\nulbra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncongregation secretary\n \n/\n \nsecretario de la congregación\n\nÂ\ni\nulra\n \n(Aiulra)\n \n(\nsee/ver:\n \nUlaia\n)\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nrider\n \n/\n \njinete\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nAras\n \nâ\ni\nulra\n \n–\n \nrider of a horse\n \n/\n \njinete de un caballo\n)\n\nAiwanaia\n \n(\nv\n)\n \n–\n \nto\n \nsing\n \n/\n \ncantar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n08/20\n):\n \nM\niriam\n \nIsrael\n \nmairka\n \nnani aikuki Jehova ra aiwanan mayunaia dukiara\n \n–\n \nM\niriam\n \ntogether with the\n \nwo\nmen of\n\nIsrael sang to Jehovah to praise him\n \n/\n \nM\ní\nriam\n \njunto con las mujeres de Israel cantaron a Jehová para alabarlo\n)\n\nAiwanpi\n \n(v-alt-imp of/de:\n \nAiwanaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(let’s all)\n \nsing\n \n/ (vamos todos) a cantar\n\nAiwans\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \nsing\n \n/ canta, cante, canten\n\nAiwawanra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nsinger\n \n/ cantante\n\nAiwawanra daknika\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nchorus of singers, group of singers, choir\n \n/ coro de cantantes,\ngrupo de cantantes, coro\n\nKli aiwananka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nchorus\n \n(\nin a song\n)\n \n/\n \ncoro\n \n(\nen una canción\n)\n\nAiya\n \n–\n \nS\nee/\nV\ner\n:\n \nAula\n\nA\nkasia dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nacacia wood\n \n/\n \nmadera de acacia\n\nAkbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto knead, to grind, to crush, to chew\n \n/ amasar, moler, aplastar, masticar\n\nAklak\n \n–\n \no’clock\n \n/ en punto\n\nAksidint\n \n(\nfg,km,bh,lv,mwb\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \naccident\n \n/ accidente\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n:\n \ndict\n,\n \ndictu\n \ninstead\n \nuse\n \n/\n \ndict, dictu\n \nen su lugar usan\n:\n \nLatawira\n)\n\nAl\n \ns\nȃ\nt\n \n–\n \nall sorts, all kinds\n \n/ todo tipo\n, toda clase\n\nAl\n \nsut\n \n–\n \ncompletely, entirely, altogether\n \n/ completamente, en conjunto",
